meta {
  name: List Courts - mismatched pair
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/courts?city=HN&area=HCM_DISTRICT_10
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  city: HN
  area: HCM_DISTRICT_10
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 400
  res.body.success: eq false
  res.body.error.code: eq INVALID_CITY_DISTRICT
}

docs {
  **Currently fails -- this is a real gap, not a stub.** `GET /courts` is implemented, but
  `ListCourtsByDistrictUseCase` never checks the city/area pair against `CITY_AREAS` the
  way `Court.create` does on the write side (see **Create Court - invalid city+district**).
  Today this returns `200` with `[]` instead of `400 INVALID_CITY_DISTRICT` -- a query for
  an impossible pair looks identical to "no courts in that district yet", which is the
  wrong signal to send a client. This assertion targets the correct behavior and will pass
  once that check is added to the use case.
}
